{"event_type":"review","id":"84b70b5e5843a29269345f4f99484741d776b5a4c8d72eb9d039a051f787ca09","occurred_at":"2026-11-22T14:55:50Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/94621b5cb8f27fa706cd9a8378ce19aa93660c202fc6c8ac2b2c74b1fec920be","sha256":"94621b5cb8f27fa706cd9a8378ce19aa93660c202fc6c8ac2b2c74b1fec920be"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0234735f43ce839a6b4d379870065753b354a6721d860af113fe6538b329a890","sha256":"0234735f43ce839a6b4d379870065753b354a6721d860af113fe6538b329a890"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8ca4683ff9d78c23b28bc353379b237e9bb2ebfede542b6481be3ddae33ee011","sha256":"8ca4683ff9d78c23b28bc353379b237e9bb2ebfede542b6481be3ddae33ee011"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/23d7c97f9e6ee77a459f129ee1cf3e6dc6aab2dc46b7a9aa720a26526c02a23f","sha256":"23d7c97f9e6ee77a459f129ee1cf3e6dc6aab2dc46b7a9aa720a26526c02a23f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/55f2a77c01695d82a45b36b7e8a40513ce870d7b4cfbb6c30dc224ee12fb5d46","sha256":"55f2a77c01695d82a45b36b7e8a40513ce870d7b4cfbb6c30dc224ee12fb5d46"}],"attempt_id":"6493a93c0fa4cb158b3503b1f41506a984eca4599d686913a65548ed16f3b433:0:1","base":"493de0cc498c655b43805cac96d50e8f05a24b28","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"2e1eb340a420d9c1725ac08b0f5709ca9522f7be","body":"**Bound the retained coverage observations.**\n\n`record_opportunity` adds one observation for each non-dry tick and never removes older entries (apps/crq-python/coverage.py:469-480). The tick timer runs every 12 minutes (apps/crq-python/ops/systemd/crq-tick.timer:4), so the ledger gains about 43,800 observations per year. Each tick deep-copies the whole ledger, including all observations, paths, and runs (coverage.py:476). The tick then saves the queue (apps/crq-python/crq.py:3682-3694). The status digest parses every observation timestamp to select the 24-hour window (coverage.py:494). Per-tick work and stored queue size therefore grow with queue age.\n\nLimit retained observations to the window that `utilization_digest` reads. Remove older entries when a new observation is recorded. The digest result must stay unchanged for any `now` at or after the last recorded tick. The retention length is a policy choice, but it must cover at least the 24-hour window.","id":"241469e9f6e8cfe6354e4d3a19163c9e44469f60663ea3667bad56dcba6b90ec","intervals":[[476,476]],"path":"apps/crq-python/coverage.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Bound the retained coverage observations."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"2e1eb340a420d9c1725ac08b0f5709ca9522f7be","body":"**Keep failure counters for released families when a counted success is recorded.**\n\n`record_legacy_success` deletes both counters for each origin unless the family is quarantined. `release_legacy_quarantine` stores the current counter values as `floors`. After such a release, a counted success can delete the counters. The next `legacy_retry_view` then reads those counters as `0`, which is below the stored floor. It denies the scope with `released counter floor missing or reduced`, even though the release run proofs are unchanged. The trigger does not need a counter of `1`. Any positive floor fails, including a normal family-failure-limit release where the counters match the six runs.\n\nSkip the deletion for released families. The retry view already applies a counted success as a new streak through the `if reset:` branch. The code comment states that persisted counters are kept.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n         family_history = queue.get(\"backfill_families\", {}).get(family, {})\n         scope_history = queue.get(\"backfill_scope_failures\", {}).get(family, {})\n-        if not family_history.get(\"quarantined\") and not scope_history.get(\"quarantined\"):\n+        released = any(r.get(\"family\") == family for r in queue.get(\"legacy_coverage_releases\", []))\n+        if not released and not family_history.get(\"quarantined\") and not scope_history.get(\"quarantined\"):\n             queue.get(\"backfill_families\", {}).pop(family, None)\n             queue.get(\"backfill_scope_failures\", {}).pop(family, None)\n```\n\n</details>","id":"6fff0049673b9ce7bb617857b89066abeb287a0396dfc08fa8ff95b492edf979","intervals":[[102,104]],"path":"apps/crq-python/coverage.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep failure counters for released families when a counted success is recorded."}],"head":"ce981e0b10d1be0ce0ea1435d6b2997933bcabd2","head_tree":"d16e28012af19cbe4667ce22a44fed8d3e652014","input_scope":[{"blob":"2e1eb340a420d9c1725ac08b0f5709ca9522f7be","intervals":[[1,507]],"path":"apps/crq-python/coverage.py"},{"blob":"6bbdbb1fcc7e85a8ea867e8099190172b24d304a","intervals":[[1,127]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_author_quota_open_cycle.py"},{"blob":"68fe3d40b47bf4b18485732aedbff0ba6b582061","intervals":[[1,432]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_crq_fixtures.py"},{"blob":"80829dc64864940fe6cc2fc66bfdd83494b85a3b","intervals":[[1,179]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_deploy_controller_fixtures.py"},{"blob":"900aa0a4d7a353cd9c3dd166d056aaa418aef9c1","intervals":[[1,90]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_host_config_fixtures.py"},{"blob":"b2c2f4bd6246e2804a399427106bb1bca563a318","intervals":[[1,43]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_host_config_render.py"},{"blob":"b3097fbd25f0da896446e8ac596d4c6d0240d265","intervals":[[1,31]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_merged_reconcile_interval.py"},{"blob":"6dec6e9343c271c990b86718fad042c3f4248491","intervals":[[1,148]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_queue_transport_lifecycle.py"}],"job_id":"6493a93c0fa4cb158b3503b1f41506a984eca4599d686913a65548ed16f3b433:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"b